<div class="mb-8">
  <Heading size="2xl" as="h1" class="mb-2">ProgressBar</Heading>
  <Text size="lg" tone="subdued" as="h2">
    A horizontal bar that visualizes progress or completion toward a goal.
  </Text>
</div>

<!-- Canonical example -->
<div class="mb-8">
  <Example source={'
    <div class="w-full max-w-md">
      <ProgressBar value=65 max=100/>
    </div>
  '}/>
</div>

<!-- Usage -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Usage</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <CodeBlock code={"<ProgressBar value=65 max=100/>\n\n<ProgressBar value=3 max=10 size=\"lg\"/>"}/>
  </div>
  <Prose class="mt-4">
    <p>
      Pass a <code>value</code> and <code>max</code> to set the fill percentage.
      The component clamps the result between 0% and 100%. The <code>size</code>
      prop controls the bar height.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- When to Use -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">When to Use</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Use ProgressBar to show how far along a process is — file uploads, profile completion,
      step-based flows, or storage usage. It gives users a quick visual read on status without
      requiring them to parse numbers.
    </p>
    <p>
      For indeterminate loading states where progress can't be measured, use a <code>Spinner</code>
      instead.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Behaviour -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Behaviour</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      The fill width is calculated as <code>value / max * 100%</code>, clamped to the 0–100%
      range. The bar renders with <code>role="progressbar"</code> and the appropriate
      <code>aria-valuenow</code>, <code>aria-valuemin</code>, and <code>aria-valuemax</code>
      attributes for screen readers.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Examples -->
<div class="flex flex-col gap-12 mb-12">
  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Sizes</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Five sizes control the bar height — from a subtle <code>xs</code> track to a bold <code>xl</code> bar.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 w-full max-w-md">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="span" class="w-6">xs</Text>
          <ProgressBar value=70 max=100 size="xs"/>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="span" class="w-6">sm</Text>
          <ProgressBar value=70 max=100 size="sm"/>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="span" class="w-6">md</Text>
          <ProgressBar value=70 max=100 size="md"/>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="span" class="w-6">lg</Text>
          <ProgressBar value=70 max=100 size="lg"/>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="span" class="w-6">xl</Text>
          <ProgressBar value=70 max=100 size="xl"/>
        </div>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Various Values</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>The fill adapts to any value/max ratio.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 w-full max-w-md">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="span" class="w-8">0%</Text>
          <ProgressBar value=0 max=100/>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="span" class="w-8">25%</Text>
          <ProgressBar value=25 max=100/>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="span" class="w-8">50%</Text>
          <ProgressBar value=50 max=100/>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="span" class="w-8">75%</Text>
          <ProgressBar value=75 max=100/>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="span" class="w-8">100%</Text>
          <ProgressBar value=100 max=100/>
        </div>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Custom Max</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Set <code>max</code> to any positive number — steps completed, bytes uploaded, etc.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 w-full max-w-md">
        <div>
          <div class="flex justify-between mb-1">
            <Text size="sm" weight="medium" as="span">Steps completed</Text>
            <Text size="sm" tone="subdued" as="span">3 of 5</Text>
          </div>
          <ProgressBar value=3 max=5 size="lg"/>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="flex justify-between mb-1">
            <Text size="sm" weight="medium" as="span">Storage used</Text>
            <Text size="sm" tone="subdued" as="span">7.2 GB of 10 GB</Text>
          </div>
          <ProgressBar value=7.2 max=10 size="lg"/>
        </div>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">In a Card</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Progress bars work well inside cards to show status within a contained context.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <Card class="w-full max-w-sm">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <div class="flex justify-between">
            <Heading size="sm" as="div">Project Alpha</Heading>
            <Badge variant="secondary">In Progress</Badge>
          </div>
          <ProgressBar value=68 max=100/>
          <Text size="xs" tone="subdued" as="p">68% complete — 12 of 18 tasks done</Text>
        </div>
      </Card>
    '}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Best Practices -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Best Practices</Heading>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-green-500/30 bg-green-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-green-600">Do</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Pair with a text label so users know what's being measured.</li>
          <li>Use <code>xs</code> or <code>sm</code> for inline or dense layouts; <code>lg</code> or <code>xl</code> when the bar is a focal element.</li>
          <li>Set <code>max</code> to reflect the actual total, not just 100.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-red-600">Don't</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Use a progress bar for indeterminate loading — use a Spinner instead.</li>
          <li>Show a full bar (100%) indefinitely — update or remove it once the task completes.</li>
          <li>Stack many progress bars without labels — they become indistinguishable.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- API Reference -->
<div>
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">API Reference</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Prop</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Type</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Values</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Default</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">value</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Float</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">any number</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">0</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">max</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Float</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">any positive number</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">100</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">size</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Symbol</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">xs, sm, md, lg, xl</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">md</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
